The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/config-io/config-io-06-draw-profile-pv-sizing.md`.

Summary of findings:
- **7 findings total** (0 critical, 1 high, 2 medium, 4 low)
- **High**: No coincidence/diversity factors applied when aggregating multiple electrical end-use loads — peak dwelling load can be overestimated by 30–60%
- **Medium**: Microwave load type missing from schedule mappings; secondary refrigerator schedule column explicitly ignored
- **Low**: PV sizing doesn't compute inverter capacity or DC/AC ratio; system losses double-count soiling when both are active; holiday lighting ignored; minor clipping computation order difference vs OCHRE

PV sizing cross-reference table confirms functional parity with OCHRE across all major categories (inverter efficiency, system losses, temperature derating, curtailment). HARES adds capabilities OCHRE lacks (automated roof geometry sizing, soiling model, shading model, flat-roof GCR).
